    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain unobstructed could significantly improve apparatus entry and egress during emergency operations. Maintaining adequate driveway width and vertical clearance along the full length of the approach would support larger emergency vehicles accessing both the main building and detached structure. Clearly marking the access point with visible address signage may assist responding units in locating the property quickly, particularly given the length of the driveway. Where perimeter fencing restricts movement around the rear of the structures, identifying or designating an alternative secondary access route could enhance responder maneuverability and support staging operations on the open terrain areas of the property."
