    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of brush and shrubs immediately adjacent to the structure would improve defensible space and may reduce the opportunity for fire to spread directly to the building. Creating and maintaining separation between scattered shrubs, trees, and the structure perimeter could further reduce fuel continuity across the property. Along the driveway, managing vegetation on both sides to maintain adequate width and vertical clearance would support firefighter access and improve conditions for emergency vehicle movement along the single access route. Given the mixed vegetation cover and brushland interface conditions surrounding the property, maintaining an open buffer zone around improvements where feasible could reduce structure exposure and support suppression operations. Periodic vegetation management within the immediate structure zone, with attention to shrubs making contact with or growing close to walls, eaves, and other structural components, would contribute to long-term wildfire resilience."
